content.thinking:
9 usages, one of which passes an **options object** (`ElMessage.error({ message, duration, showClose })`). So `notify` must accept either a string or an options object.

Design: 
```js
/** 所有提示走这里：测试里没有 document，把 notify 换掉就能断言"用户看到了什么" */
notify(type, options) {
  ElMessage[type](options);
}
```
Then replace `ElMessage.success(X)` → `this.notify('success', X)`, `ElMessage.error({...})` → `this.notify('error', {...})`.

Careful at line 734: inside `.catch((e) => ElMessage.error(...))` — arrow function keeps `this` ✓.

Let me do it with a script (regex-based) + assert counts, then add the method.

